# Lizard, Connors's Curse: "When Lizard, Connors's Curse enters, up to one other target creature loses all abilities and becomes a green
# Lizard creature with base power and toughness 4/4." Bot2's Llanowar Elves (a 1/1 Creature - Elf Druid with "{T}: Add {G}") is the only other
# creature, so it is the target. It becomes a Creature - Lizard alone (the Elf and Druid types are replaced, CR 205.1b), green, 4/4, and
# the effect does not end at end of turn (the ruling): on Bot2's turn 4 it is still a 4/4 Lizard, untapped and past summoning sickness, and
# its "{T}: Add {G}" is not offered - it has no abilities.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald x4
Lizard, Connors's Curse
Forest x2
Forest x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#3.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#4.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lizard, Connors's Curse.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 4
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Toughness = 4
! Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Types = Creature
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Subtypes = Lizard
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Colors = Green
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 4
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Lizard, Connors's Curse.Power = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Lizard, Connors's Curse.Toughness = 5
